    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0563" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150.071 Control/194</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Swedish Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Boström</hi>)</head>
                <p>In view of the fact that a new Bill (S. 379), to provide for the deportation of
                    certain alien seamen and for other purposes, has now been introduced by Senator
                        King,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d345-f1"/> the Minister of Sweden begs
                    respectfully to call attention to his memorandum of March 9, 1934,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d345-f2"/> left at the Department of State on the same date.</p>
                <p>The Minister would highly appreciate it if the facts therein set forth could be
                    given due consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-22">January 22,
                            1935</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d345-f1" n="2" xml:id="d345-f1-content">
                <p>Introduced on January 7, 1935, by Senator William H. King of Utah; <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Congressional Record</hi>, vol. 79, pt. 1, p. 136.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d345-f2" n="3" xml:id="d345-f2-content">
